                                {
                                    "name": "core/paragraph",
                                    "attributes": {
                                        "content": "Le French Cancan",
                                        "textColor": "gold",
                                        "fontSize": "small",
                                        "fontFamily": "affiche",
                                        "style": { "typography": { "textTransform": "uppercase", "letterSpacing": "0.28em" } }
                                    }
                                },
                                {
                                    "name": "core/heading",
                                    "attributes": {
                                        "level": 2,
                                        "content": "The dance that shocked, then conquered",
                                        "fontSize": "xx-large",
                                        "fontFamily": "boulevard"
                                    }
                                },
                                {
                                    "name": "core/paragraph",
                                    "attributes": {
                                        "content": "The cancan began as the <em>chahut</em> — a rowdy, improvised quadrille from the working-class dance halls. At the Moulin Rouge it became a profession: high kicks, cartwheels, jump-splits, and petticoats whipped up like sea foam."
                                    }
                                },
                                {
                                    "name": "core/paragraph",
                                    "attributes": {
                                        "content": "Its stars went by legend-names — La Goulue (“The Glutton”), Jane Avril, Nini Pattes-en-l’Air — and a painter named Henri de Toulouse-Lautrec printed them into immortality. His 1891 poster for the house remains one of the most famous images ever made."
                                    }
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
